    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Union-find algorithm. This data structure takes connections between two elements, and finds all of the connected components and their sizes. A &quot;component&quot; is represented by a single representative item.</para>
<para>See:</para>
<para>Tarjan, Robert Endre (1975). &quot;Efficiency of a Good But Not Linear
    Set Union Algorithm&quot;. JACM. 22 (2): 215–225. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
